IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part V: regs 90 and 91, Electronic Systems.
-- Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt. The text is an unofficial rendering;
-- nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld): reg 90 is a duty on anyone who gives the Commission information (the Commission holds the correlative claim);
-- reg 91(1) to (3) are deeming provisions that give a claimant who claims by telephone or other electronic means the same standing as a claimant who claims
-- on paper (a power, with the Commission subject to it); reg 91(5) makes a person who knowingly interferes with the electronic systems liable
-- to be refused access to them (the Commission holds the power). Section 38 of the Act (false or misleading statements; penalty) is piece ei2's and section 135 (the offence; punishment) is piece ei4's;
-- section 50 (the information a claim requires) and sections 48 and 49 (the claims) are piece ei2's, and section 152.1 (the self-employed person's claim) is piece ei5's:
-- none is encoded here, and each is taken as a plain input where it matters.

§ `Regulations Part V - Electronic Systems`

§§ `Reg 90 - information in a form and manner approved by the Commission`

-- Where any information is provided to the Commission in electronic or other form for the purposes of the Act or the regulations, it shall be provided in a form and manner approved by the Commission.
-- Whether the Commission has approved a form and manner is the Commission's judgment, taken as a BOOLEAN input.
-- src:1686 | 90 Where any information is provided to the Commission in electronic or other form for the purposes of the Act or the regulations made under the Act, it shall be provided in a form and manner approved by the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 90 (src:1686)
GIVEN `information is provided to the Commission in electronic or other form for the purposes of the Act or the regulations made under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 90 the information must be provided in a form and manner approved by the Commission` IF
    `information is provided to the Commission in electronic or other form for the purposes of the Act or the regulations made under the Act`

-- src:1686 | 90 Where any information is provided to the Commission in electronic or other form for the purposes of the Act or the regulations made under the Act, it shall be provided in a form and manner approved by the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 90 (src:1686)
GIVEN `information is provided to the Commission in electronic or other form for the purposes of the Act or the regulations made under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form and manner is one approved by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 90 the information is provided as the Commission requires` IF
        (NOT (`reg 90 the information must be provided in a form and manner approved by the Commission` `information is provided to the Commission in electronic or other form for the purposes of the Act or the regulations made under the Act`))
    OR  `the form and manner is one approved by the Commission`

§§ `Reg 91(1) - a claim by telephone or other electronic means`

-- A claimant who makes an initial claim, or a claim for a week of unemployment, by telephone or other electronic means, and provides the information required by s 50 of the Act, is deemed
-- (a) to have expressed an intention to make a claim and to have made one for the purposes of s 48, 49 or 152.1 of the Act, as the case may be; and
-- (b) to have supplied the information recorded on the dated printout from the Commission's computerized benefit pay system as responses to the questions posed by the interactive response system.
-- src:1687 | 91 (1) A claimant who makes an initial claim for benefits, or a claim for benefits for a week of unemployment, by telephone or other electronic means, and provides the information required by section 50 of the Act, is deemed
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 91(1) (src:1687)
GIVEN `the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits, or a claim for benefits for a week of unemployment, by telephone or other electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant provides the information required by section 50 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 50 of the Act (piece ei2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 91(1) the claim is made by telephone or other electronic means with the information section 50 requires` IF
        `the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits, or a claim for benefits for a week of unemployment, by telephone or other electronic means`
    AND `the claimant provides the information required by section 50 of the Act`

-- src:1688 | (a) to have expressed an intention to make a claim for benefits and to have made such a claim for the purposes of section 48, 49 or 152.1 of the Act, as the case may be; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 91(1)(a) (src:1688)
GIVEN `the claim is made by telephone or other electronic means with the information section 50 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 91(1)(a) the claimant is deemed to have expressed an intention to make a claim and to have made it for the purposes of section 48, 49 or 152.1 of the Act` IF
    `the claim is made by telephone or other electronic means with the information section 50 requires`

-- src:1689 | (b) to have supplied the information recorded on the dated printout from the Commission's computerized benefit pay system as responses to the questions posed by the interactive response system by telephone or other electronic means.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 91(1)(b) (src:1689)
GIVEN `the claim is made by telephone or other electronic means with the information section 50 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 91(1)(b) the claimant is deemed to have supplied the information on the dated printout as responses to the questions of the interactive response system` IF
    `the claim is made by telephone or other electronic means with the information section 50 requires`

§§ `Reg 91(2) - deemed to have signed the claim`

-- A claimant who provides their Social Insurance Number and the following information by telephone or other electronic means is deemed to have signed the claim:
-- (a) for an initial claim, their date of birth and, if the initial claim is made by electronic means, the maiden name of the claimant's mother;
-- (b) for a claim for a week of unemployment, their personal identification number.
-- "If the initial claim is made by electronic means" is read against a claim made by telephone: the maiden name is asked only of the claim made by other electronic means.
-- src:1690 | (2) A claimant who provides their Social Insurance Number and the following information by telephone or other electronic means is deemed to have signed their respective claim for benefit:
-- src:1691 | (a) in the case of an initial claim for benefits, their date of birth and, if the initial claim is made by electronic means, the maiden name of the claimant's mother; and
-- src:1692 | (b) in the case of a claim for benefits for a week of unemployment, their personal identification number.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 91(2) (src:1690-1692)
DECLARE `er5 Kind of claim made by telephone or other electronic means` IS ONE OF
    `er5 an initial claim for benefits`
    `er5 a claim for benefits for a week of unemployment`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 91(2) (src:1690-1692)
GIVEN kind IS A `er5 Kind of claim made by telephone or other electronic means`
      `the claimant provides their Social Insurance Number by telephone or other electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant provides their date of birth by telephone or other electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the initial claim is made by electronic means other than telephone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant provides the maiden name of the claimant's mother by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant provides their personal identification number by telephone or other electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 91(2) the claimant is deemed to have signed the claim` IF
        `the claimant provides their Social Insurance Number by telephone or other electronic means`
    AND (   CONSIDER kind
            WHEN `er5 an initial claim for benefits` THEN
                    `the claimant provides their date of birth by telephone or other electronic means`
                AND ((NOT `the initial claim is made by electronic means other than telephone`) OR `the claimant provides the maiden name of the claimant's mother by electronic means`)
            WHEN `er5 a claim for benefits for a week of unemployment` THEN
                `the claimant provides their personal identification number by telephone or other electronic means`)

§§ `Reg 91(3) - the day the claim is made`

-- A claim made by the means referred to in subsection (1) is deemed to have been made on the day that the information is received and recorded by the Commission's computerized benefit pay system.
-- For a claim made by other means the text says nothing here, and the rule returns NOTHING.
-- src:1693 | (3) A claim for benefits that is made by the means referred to in subsection (1) is deemed to have been made on the day that the information is received and recorded by the Commission's computerized benefit pay system.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 91(3) (src:1693)
GIVEN `the claim is made by the means referred to in subsection 91(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the information is received and recorded by the Commission's computerized benefit pay system` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 91(3) the day on which the claim is deemed to have been made` IS
    IF `the claim is made by the means referred to in subsection 91(1)`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the information is received and recorded by the Commission's computerized benefit pay system`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Reg 91(4) and (5) - sections 38 and 135 of the Act and the electronic systems`

-- For greater certainty, sections 38 and 135 of the Act apply to a declaration made by electronic means.
-- src:1694 | (4) For greater certainty, sections 38 and 135 of the Act apply to a declaration made by electronic means.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 91(4) (src:1694)
GIVEN `the declaration is made by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 91(4) sections 38 and 135 of the Act apply to the declaration` IF
    `the declaration is made by electronic means`

-- The acts and omissions specified in ss 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act are deemed to include those of a person who knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic
-- systems used in the administration of the Act; the penalty in s 38(2) and the punishment in s 135(3) are deemed to include the right to refuse access to those systems to such a person.
-- src:1695 | (5) The acts and omissions specified in subsections 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act are deemed to include the acts and omissions of a person who knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used in the administration of the Act, and the penalty provided for by subsection 38(2) of the Act and the punishment provided for by subsection 135(3) of the Act are deemed to include the right to refuse access to those electronic systems to such a person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 91(5) (src:1695)
GIVEN `the person knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used in the administration of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 91(5) the act is deemed to be an act or omission specified in subsections 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act` IF
    `the person knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used in the administration of the Act`

-- src:1695 | (5) The acts and omissions specified in subsections 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act are deemed to include the acts and omissions of a person who knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used in the administration of the Act, and the penalty provided for by subsection 38(2) of the Act and the punishment provided for by subsection 135(3) of the Act are deemed to include the right to refuse access to those electronic systems to such a person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 91(5) (src:1695)
GIVEN `the person knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used in the administration of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 91(5) the penalty and the punishment include the right to refuse the person access to the electronic systems` IF
    `the person knowingly attempts to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used in the administration of the Act`
